# Research: in-progress-phase-columns

### Task Slice

- **Classification:** a read-side feature for the web UI's kanban board. It touches `internal/task/view.go` (the board snapshot), `internal/web/view.go` (the view model), `internal/web/templates/_board.html` and `_card.html`, `internal/web/assets/input.css` plus the generated `static/app.css`, and the `CLAUDE.md` "Web UI" section. No tool, schema or frontmatter change is involved.
- **Scope covered:**
  - the board render path, from the HTTP route to the templates;
  - how columns, cards, nested subtasks, the danger zone, branch chips and blocked flags are built today;
  - how attached files are stored and listed, what it costs, and what file names the workflow skills actually write;
  - service locking and the twin discipline;
  - polling, the Tailwind build and embedded assets;
  - existing tests and helpers, and the baseline test status on this machine;
  - the current CSS layout and breakpoints.
- **Documents loaded:**
  - `CLAUDE.md` (Web UI section at lines 226-239, Package boundary at lines 29-34, Concurrency, Subtasks);
  - `README.md` lines 80-100 (Web Dashboard);
  - `_design.md` (resolution and verified_at only; nothing relevant here);
  - `.claude/skills/research|begin_task|workflow|implementation/SKILL.md`;
  - `plugins/mcp-task-manager/skills/*` (diffed against `.claude/skills`), `plugins/mcp-task-manager/commands/*.md` and `scripts/sync-skills.sh`;
  - the earlier web UI design artifact `tasks/web-ui-kanban-module/design.md` (grepped for column, poll and layout decisions);
  - `internal/app/instructions.md`.
  - There is no `doc/` directory. `docs/plans/*` contains nothing about the web UI.

### Confirmed Facts

#### 1. Rendering path (route → handler → resolver → snapshot → view model → template → assets)

- **Routes.** Only GET patterns are registered in `internal/web/server.go`:
  - `GET /{$}` → `h.board` (line 58)
  - `GET /board` → `h.boardFragment` (line 59, the htmx poll target)
  - `GET /tasks/{id}` (line 60) and `GET /tasks/{id}/panel` (line 61)
  - `GET /static/` (line 62)
  - `GET /healthz` (line 63)
  - `NewHandler` is at `internal/web/server.go:54-65`.
- **Poll interval.** `DefaultPollSeconds = 5` (`internal/web/server.go:15`). `Deps.PollSeconds` overrides it (`server.go:29-30`), and `withDefaults` applies the default when it is ≤0 (`server.go:33-47`). The production wiring in `internal/app/app.go:70` and `:110` never sets `PollSeconds`, so the poll is always 5 s.
- **Handlers never resolve.** `Deps.Project` is documented as "Wire this to Resolver.Current, never to Resolver.Get" (`internal/web/server.go:19-23`). `internal/app/app.go:70` and `:110` pass `resolver.Current`. `Resolver.Current()` only reads the cached value under its own mutex (`internal/project/resolver.go:112-116`).
- **Handlers:**
  - `board` renders `boardPage` / `layout.html` with `h.boardView()` (`internal/web/handlers.go:15-17`).
  - `boardFragment` renders `_board.html`, or `_unresolved.html` when `!view.Project.Resolved` (`handlers.go:21-28`).
  - `boardView()` calls `h.Project()`; if nothing is resolved it returns `unresolvedBoardView`. Otherwise it calls `resolved.Service.BoardSnapshot()` and then `newBoardView(snap, resolved.Config, h.Now(), h.PollSeconds)` (`handlers.go:55-66`). A snapshot error is logged and falls back to the placeholder (`handlers.go:61-63`).
  - `render` buffers the output, then writes it; a template error becomes a 500 (`handlers.go:102-112`).
- **`BoardSnapshot` has a second caller.** `handlers.go:87-98` (`titles`) calls `svc.BoardSnapshot()` to resolve relation titles for the detail view. It runs only when the task has relations (`handlers.go:80-83`). Any added cost in `BoardSnapshot` is therefore also paid by those detail views. These are the only two callers of `BoardSnapshot` outside tests (grep of `internal/`).
- **Service snapshot.**
  - `Service.BoardSnapshot()` locks `s.mu` and delegates to the unlocked `boardSnapshot()` (`internal/task/view.go:49-53`).
  - `boardSnapshot()` calls `s.index.All()`. It fills `Subtasks` (grouped by parent id) and `Counts` (per-parent total/done) in one loop, then sets `Blocked = s.blockedMap(ids)` (`view.go:55-82`).
  - Snapshot type `BoardSnapshot{Tasks []*Task; Subtasks map[string][]*Task; Blocked map[string][]BlockingInfo; Counts map[string]SubtaskCount; TakenAt time.Time}` is at `view.go:21-35`. `Tasks` holds "every active task, top-level and subtask alike, without descriptions (index entries only)" (`view.go:24-26`).
- **View model.** `newBoardView` is documented as "Pure: everything it needs was already read under the service lock" (`internal/web/view.go:131-133`). It:
  1. builds one `CardView` per task (`view.go:140-144`);
  2. places each card in the column of its own status, or nests it in its parent's card when the parent has the same status (`view.go:146-162`);
  3. builds the columns from the fixed `columns` slice (`view.go:164-179`);
  4. builds the danger zone (`view.go:181-192`).
- **Templates:**
  - `board.html` lays out the board next to a `#panel` aside, and includes `_board.html` or `_unresolved.html` (`internal/web/templates/board.html:1-13`).
  - `_board.html` is the poll container: `<div id="board" hx-get="/board" hx-trigger="every {{ .PollSeconds }}s" hx-swap="outerHTML">` (`_board.html:1`). Every 5 s the whole board, columns included, is replaced.
  - `_unresolved.html:1` carries the same poll attributes.
  - `layout.html` loads `/static/app.css`, `/static/htmx.min.js` and `/static/app.js` (`layout.html:7-9`).
- **Template parsing.**
  - `fragments` is `ParseFS("templates/_*.html")`.
  - Each page set is `layout.html` + the page + `templates/_*.html` (`internal/web/templates.go:19-31`).
  - A new `_*.html` partial is therefore picked up by both sets through the glob.
  - No funcMap is registered, deliberately: "every field is already a plain string" and there is no `template.HTML` (`templates.go:11-18`).
- **Static assets.**
  - `//go:embed static/app.css static/htmx.min.js static/app.js` names each file explicitly (`internal/web/assets.go:9-13`).
  - They are served with `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` (`assets.go:17-27`).
  - `app.js` is a single delegated click listener for `[data-copy]` that sends no request (`internal/web/static/app.js:37-53`).

#### 2. Data structures; how columns, cards, flags and subtasks are built

- **`BoardView`** = `{Project ProjectView; Columns []ColumnView; DangerZone []DangerItem; PollSeconds int; Generated string}` (`internal/web/view.go:27-33`).
- **`ColumnView`** = `{Status, Title string; Count int; Cards []CardView}` (`view.go:35-41`). There is no sub-column or grouping field.
- **`CardView` fields** (`view.go:43-68`): ID, Title, Priority, Type, Status, PriorityRank, IsSubtask, ParentID, Blocked, Blockers, SubtaskTotal, SubtaskDone, Resolution, InProgress, UpdatedAgo, Branch, Subtasks, and the unexported `createdAt`, used for sorting only. There is no phase or files field.
- **The column abstraction is a Go slice, not template branching.**
  - `var columns = []struct{Status task.Status; Title string}{{todo,"To do"},{in_progress,"In progress"},{done,"Done"}}` (`view.go:119-127`).
  - The template ranges over `.Columns` with one generic `<section class="column">` per column. There is no per-status branch in `_board.html` (`_board.html:13-28`).
  - Each column header shows `dot dot-{{ .Status }}`, the title, and a `chip chip-muted` count (`_board.html:16-20`). An empty column renders `<p ...>empty</p>` (`_board.html:22-24`).
- **Column count.** `Count` is the number of tasks in that status, nested subtasks included, not the number of cards (`view.go:167-172`). The test `TestSubtaskNestsWhenParentShareColumn` asserts "the count is tasks, not cards" (`internal/web/view_test.go:102-104`).
- **Sorting.** `sortCards` orders by priority rank, then `createdAt` (oldest first), then ID (`view.go:345-356`). It is applied to root cards per column (`view.go:165-166`) and to nested kids (`view.go:159-162`).
- **Subtask placement.** A card nests under its parent only when `parent.Status == card.Status` (`view.go:149-158`); otherwise it is a standalone root card with `IsSubtask`/`ParentID` set (`view.go:224-225`).
  - The key is status equality only.
  - Starting a subtask auto-starts a `todo` parent (`internal/task/service.go:668`; CLAUDE.md Subtasks). In-progress parents with in-progress subtasks are therefore the common case, and those subtasks nest inside the parent card in the In progress column.
  - The parent card's `SubtaskTotal`/`SubtaskDone` come from `snap.Counts` (`view.go:236-238`).
- **Card flags** (`newCardView`, `view.go:216-240`):
  - `InProgress = t.Status == StatusInProgress` (`view.go:227`);
  - `Blocked`/`Blockers` come from `snap.Blocked[t.ID]` (`view.go:232-235`);
  - `Branch = cardBranch(t)`, which is `FinalBranch` if set, else `Branch` (`view.go:244-249`).
- **Card markup** (`_card.html`):
  - `<article class="card {{ if .InProgress }}card-live{{ end }} {{ if .Blocked }}card-blocked{{ end }}">` (line 1);
  - the main link carries `hx-get="/tasks/{{ .ID }}/panel" hx-target="#panel" hx-swap="innerHTML" hx-push-url="/tasks/{{ .ID }}"` (lines 2-7);
  - the ID and `↳ parent` meta, plus the priority chip (lines 8-12); the title (line 13);
  - the chips: type, resolution, `N/M subtasks`, `chip-live` "in progress", `chip-blocked` with blocker tooltip, and UpdatedAgo (lines 14-21);
  - the branch row via `{{ template "branch" .Branch }}` (lines 24-28);
  - nested subtasks as compact links showing ID, title, a blocked chip and the priority chip. They have no branch chip and no in-progress chip (lines 30-46).
- **Branch template.** The `"branch"` template defined in `_branch.html:2-5` is a `code.chip` plus `<button class="copy-btn" data-copy=...>`.
- **Danger zone.**
  - Built from every task with status `in_progress` (subtasks included) as `DangerItem{ID, Title, Type, UpdatedAgo}`, sorted by ID (`view.go:181-192`; type at `view.go:77-83`).
  - Rendered as an amber banner above the grid, only when non-empty (`_board.html:2-11`).
  - Card highlighting is the `card-live` class plus the `chip-live` chip (`_card.html:1`, `:18`).
- **Placeholder.** `unresolvedBoardView(poll)` returns a `BoardView` with only `PollSeconds` set (`view.go:199-201`).
- **No template uses `ColumnView.Status` except for the `dot-{{ .Status }}` class** (`_board.html:17`).

#### 3. Attached files: storage API, cost, names actually written

- **Service-level interface.** `FileStorage` is `{WriteFile; ReadFile; ListFiles(taskID) ([]string, error)}` (`internal/task/service.go:87-96`). It is held in `Service.fileStorage` (`service.go:102`).
  - In production it is the same `*MarkdownStorage` as storage and archive (`internal/project/resolver.go:160`).
  - Many unit tests pass `nil` for fileStorage, for example `internal/task/service_test.go:373`, `:396`, `:501`, `internal/task/resolution_test.go:11` and `internal/task/current_test.go:40`.
  - `detail()` guards against nil with `if s.fileStorage != nil` (`internal/task/view.go:114-118`).
- **`MarkdownStorage.ListFiles(taskID)`** (`internal/storage/files.go:105-125`):
  - calls `resolveTaskDir`: an `os.Stat` of `{dir}/{id}/{id}.md`, falling back to `os.Stat` of the archive path (`files.go:130-138`);
  - then one `os.ReadDir(dir)`;
  - skips subdirectories and the `{id}.md` record file;
  - returns `entry.Name()` verbatim. `os.ReadDir` returns entries sorted by name.
  - Cost per task: one or two `stat` calls plus one `ReadDir`.
  - It does not filter `*.tmp`. `writeFileAtomic` writes `<path>.tmp` and then renames it (`internal/storage/markdown.go:102-112`).
- **Name handling.**
  - No case normalization or extension handling exists anywhere. `validateFilename` only rejects empty names, `/`, `\`, `..`, and `{id}.md` on write (`files.go:14-40`).
  - The mock `ListFiles` in task tests iterates a map, so its order is random (`internal/task/service_test.go:141-147`).
- **Callers of file listing.**
  - `Service.ListTaskFiles` (exported, locked) has no unlocked twin. It calls `s.get` and then `s.fileStorage.ListFiles` (`service.go:345-355`).
  - `detail()` calls `s.fileStorage.ListFiles` directly (`view.go:114-118`).
  - The CLI calls it at `internal/cli/commands.go:458` and the MCP tool at `internal/tools/files.go:104`.
- **Writing a file does not touch the task record or the index.**
  - `WriteTaskFile` checks `s.index.Get(taskID)` and then calls `fileStorage.WriteFile` only (`service.go:318-331`).
  - `UpdatedAt` is unchanged, so the card's "x ago" does not move when a phase file is written.
  - The index staleness check only stats `{id}/{id}.md` mtimes and counts task dirs (`internal/storage/index.go:209-245`; `After(idx.builtAt)` at line 231; count check at line 240). Attached-file writes are invisible to the index.
- **The board snapshot already touches the filesystem beyond the in-memory index:**
  - `index.All()` calls `syncIfStale()` (`index.go:286-287`), which runs `isStaleOnDisk`: one `os.ReadDir(tasksDir)` plus one `os.Stat` per task dir (`index.go:209-237`), and a full `Rebuild` when stale (`index.go:198-204`);
  - `blockedMap` calls `s.index.AllBlockers()`, which runs `syncIfStale` again (`index.go:609-610`);
  - its `lookup` calls `s.index.Get(id)` once per distinct blocker target (`view.go:148-160`), and each of those runs `syncIfStale` plus `storage.Load`, a task-file read (`index.go:261-272`).
  - Today the snapshot never calls `ListFiles` or any `fileStorage` method (`view.go:55-82`).
  - The earlier design doc claimed "zero file reads on the steady path" (`tasks/web-ui-kanban-module/design.md:815`). The code does read task files when blockers exist, as shown above; the code wins.
  - Precedent: the earlier design declined per-card description excerpts because they "would cost one file read per card per poll" (`tasks/web-ui-kanban-module/design.md:92`).
- **Names the current workflow writes** (`.claude/skills/begin_task/SKILL.md`; identical in `plugins/mcp-task-manager/skills/begin_task/SKILL.md`, since `diff -r` shows only the extra `superpowers-workflow` dir in plugins):
  - `task`, at line 17: "Write a `task` file … a `.md` document" — the file is named `task`, its content is Markdown;
  - `research` (line 36), `design` (line 46), `plan` (line 56), `implementation` (line 66).
  - The plugin skills are the source; `.claude/skills` is a generated mirror (`scripts/sync-skills.sh:1-12`).
  - Each phase file is saved after its phase finishes: `research` at the end of step 2, `design` at the end of step 3, `plan` at the end of step 4, `implementation` after implementation (`begin_task/SKILL.md:36,46,56,66`).
  - `superpowers-workflow` and `plugins/.../commands/*.md` do not name any attached files.
- **Names actually present on disk** (scan of `tasks/`):
  - `tasks/git-branch-per-task/` has `task`, `research`, `design`, `plan`, `implementation`, no extension. Its status is `done`.
  - `tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/` has `task` only. Its status is `in_progress`, and it is the current task in `tasks/.users/igor.cwer/current_task`.
  - `tasks/web-ui-kanban-module/` has `task.md`, `research.md`, `design.md`, `plan.md`, with a `.md` extension. Its status is `done`.
  - The extension came from the old `create_task` skill, which wrote `.tasks/{task-name}/task.md`, `research.md`, `design.md`, `plan.md` and `implementation.md`. Commit `e989d62` renamed it to `begin_task` and switched to suffix-less names (`git show e989d62`, removed lines).
  - None of the 87 archived tasks carries a workflow file.
- **Case sensitivity.** All skill texts use lowercase names. Nothing in the code lowercases names, and this machine's NTFS checkout is case-insensitive at the filesystem level.

#### 4. Locking and the twin discipline

- One `sync.Mutex` sits on `Service`. The discipline comment reads: "exported methods lock once on entry and delegate to an unexported, unlocked twin. Service methods NEVER call each other's exported forms … add it in this shape or TestServiceNoSelfDeadlock will fail" (`internal/task/service.go:113-123`).
- `Config`, `EnsureProjectExists`, `ProjectFound` and `BranchingEnabled` are deliberately unlocked, because they read write-once fields (`service.go:143-172`; `view.go:178-183`).
- **`TestServiceNoSelfDeadlock`** (`internal/task/concurrency_test.go:105-149`):
  - it is a hand-written list of calls under a 10 s watchdog that panics on deadlock;
  - it covers `BoardSnapshot` (line 138), `Detail` (line 139), `ListTaskFiles` (line 133) and others;
  - a new exported method is only guarded if it is added to that list.
- **`TestServiceRace`** runs `BoardSnapshot`, `Detail` and `ListTaskFiles` concurrently with writers, including `WriteTaskFile`, over unlocked map mocks (`concurrency_test.go:59-100`). Its service is `newConcurrentService()` with `newMockFileStorage()` (`concurrency_test.go:17-26`).
- During `BoardSnapshot` the mutex is held for the whole of `index.All()` and `blockedMap` (`view.go:49-53`). Git flows run while holding the same lock, with a 60 s timeout per git command (CLAUDE.md Concurrency). A board poll waits behind them.

